0..76 Comment "// A category with families as a theory whose sorts depend on earlier sorts."
77..154 Comment "// Contexts and substitutions form a category, a type lives in a context, and"
155..229 Comment "// a term has a type in a context (Huang and Angiuli, _Fat Cell Structures"
230..280 Comment "// and Generalized Algebraic Theories_, LICS 2026,"
281..325 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.LICS.2026.58, § 1.1)."
326..328 Comment "//"
329..399 Comment "// Dependent type theory states its syntax and its models through this"
400..472 Comment "// signature. `Tm(g, a)` reads `a` at the sort `Ty(g)`, so a term\'s sort"
473..549 Comment "// names the context of its type. Comprehension extends a context by a type,"
550..609 Comment "// and substitution moves types and terms between contexts."
610..612 Comment "//"
613..686 Comment "// The standard model reads a context as a type, a type in it as a family"
687..759 Comment "// over it, and a term as a section of that family. The block\'s value of"
760..834 Comment "// `Theory` keeps each index as data, so a program reads it back. The laws"
835..899 Comment "// are refused in the twin until the units that admit them land."
900..902 Comment "//"
903..917 Comment "// - see: #522"
918..933 Comment "// - see: #5016"
934..949 Comment "// - see: #5017"
951..1024 Comment "/// The CwF signature: four sorts, each over the sorts before it, and the"
1025..1068 Comment "/// operations of a category with families."
